# The compatibility fixture is a byte-frozen artefact, not source.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is `input` on the maintainer's machine and unset on the CI
# runners, so without this git would normalise `notes/005-crlf.md` to LF on the
# way in and the test that exists to prove CRLF survives a round trip would be
# testing LF. `-text` turns off end-of-line conversion and diffing heuristics for
# the whole tree, which is what "frozen" has to mean if it means anything.
tests/fixtures/vault-v1/** -text
